{"type": "tool_call", "n": 65, "ts": 1790155288.169037, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "US OPERATING EXPENSE FLUX \u2013 MARCH 2026 vs FEBRUARY 2026 (USD)\nPrepared by: senior accountant, 2026-04-03. Status: PARTIAL \u2013 see \"Limitations\" at the end.\n\n1. FLUX TABLE (period activity, debit minus credit)\nAcct  Line                          Feb 2026     Mar 2026     $ Change    % Change  Flag\n5000  Hosting & Infrastructure      31,301.80    40,948.20    +9,646.40   +30.8%    EXPLAIN\n6000  Salaries & Wages             183,800.38   184,465.91      +665.53    +0.4%\n6010  Payroll Taxes                 14,060.73    14,111.64       +50.91    +0.4%\n6100  Rent                          14,500.00    14,500.00         0.00     0.0%\n6110  Utilities                        919.82       922.22        +2.40    +0.3%\n6200  Software Subscriptions         4,139.80     3,339.50      -800.30   -19.3%    <$5k, not flagged\n6300  Travel                           785.40     7,158.41    +6,373.01  +811.4%    EXPLAIN\n6310  Meals & Entertainment            114.32        49.75       -64.57   -56.5%    <$5k\n6320  Training & Conferences           542.56         0.00      -542.56  -100.0%    <$5k\n6400  Marketing Programs             7,898.14    29,686.00   +21,787.86  +275.9%    EXPLAIN\n6600  Office Supplies                  197.75       281.47       +83.72   +42.3%    <$5k\n6800  Depreciation                   3,425.00         0.00    -3,425.00  -100.0%    <$5k but see note\n6900  Bank Fees                         65.00         0.00       -65.00  -100.0%    <$5k\nZero activity both months: 5100, 5200, 6020, 6030, 6120, 6410, 6500, 6510, 6520, 6550, 6700, 6950, 7000, 7100, 7200.\nTotal expense (all lines above): Feb 261,750.70 -> Mar 295,477.10, +33,726.40 (+12.9%).\n\n2. LINES MEETING BOTH THRESHOLDS (>10% AND >$5,000)\n\n(a) 5000 Hosting & Infrastructure: +$9,646.40 (+30.8%) \u2013 DRIVER IDENTIFIED, SUPPORT ATTACHED IN LEDGER\n  Feb: JE-00125 (2026-02-03) Stackline Cloud inv STA-12523, production cloud infrastructure, $31,301.80.\n  Mar: JE-00232 (2026-03-03) Stackline Cloud inv STA-98877, production cloud infrastructure, $31,148.20 (recurring, -$153.60 vs Feb, immaterial).\n       JE-00258 (2026-03-14) Stackline Cloud inv SC-M-2203, \"one-time data migration\", $9,800.00.\n  Explanation: the recurring production hosting charge is flat month over month. Essentially the entire variance is the $9,800 one-time data migration billed by Stackline Cloud on 3/14. Both March entries show has_support=true in the ledger.\n  Does it hold up? Directionally yes \u2013 the variance is fully explained by a single identifiable non-recurring invoice. Caveat: I was not able to open the SC-M-2203 support document itself (see Limitations), so I have NOT independently confirmed (i) that the invoice is dated/for services in March, (ii) that a one-time migration is properly an expense rather than a capitalizable implementation cost, or (iii) that it is not an accrual already booked in 2100 (which would double-count). Recommend the controller/reviewer open the DOC behind JE-00258 to confirm before signing off. Expect 5000 to revert to ~$31k in April.\n\n(b) 6300 Travel: +$6,373.01 (+811%) \u2013 DRIVER NOT YET VERIFIED\n  Feb activity $785.40; Mar activity $7,158.41. I was unable to pull the March 6300 ledger detail before the session budget was exhausted, so I cannot cite the specific transactions. This line should be treated as OPEN in the flux. Given the size of the jump vs. a run rate under $1k, the reviewer should look for (i) a single large trip/conference-related booking (note 6320 Training & Conferences went to zero in March \u2013 possible reclass/miscoding between 6300 and 6320), (ii) credit-card feed items coded to Travel, or (iii) an expense-report batch covering multiple months.\n\n(c) 6400 Marketing Programs: +$21,787.86 (+276%) \u2013 DRIVER NOT YET VERIFIED\n  Feb activity $7,898.14; Mar activity $29,686.00. The March figure is a round number, which is consistent with one or two large vendor invoices or an accrual rather than a series of small program spends. I was unable to pull the 6400 ledger detail. Treat as OPEN. Reviewer should confirm the March entries have invoices/contracts attached, that the service period is March (not a prepaid annual program or event deposit that belongs in 1200 Prepaid Expenses), and that nothing is duplicated between an AP bill and a 2100 accrual.\n\n3. ITEMS BELOW THRESHOLD BUT WORTH NOTING\n  - 6800 Depreciation: $0 in March vs $3,425 in Feb. This is not a real variance \u2013 the \"Record depreciation\" checklist item is still OPEN for US March. Once the standard entry posts, this line will be flat. Flux should be re-run after that entry.\n  - 6900 Bank Fees $0 in March vs $65 in Feb \u2013 likely the bank-fee line has not yet been booked from the March statement; \"Bank reconciliations\" is also still open.\n  - 6200 Software Subscriptions down $800 (-19%): \"Amortize prepaid software\" checklist item is still open, so March prepaid amortization has probably not been recorded. The line will likely rise once it posts.\n  - Also still open on the US checklist: Accrue unpaid payroll, AP cutoff review, Intercompany reconciliation. Because AP cutoff and accruals are not done, all three flagged lines (especially 6400 and 5000) could still move. This flux is a preliminary view.\n\n4. ENTRIES POSTED / EXCEPTIONS FLAGGED\n  None. I did not post any journal entries or flag exceptions, because I could not obtain the supporting detail needed to justify either action for 6300 and 6400, and the 5000 driver is supported in the ledger pending document review.\n\n5. LIMITATIONS (please read)\n  The session's tool-call budget was exhausted after retrieving the account balances for all 27 US expense accounts and the 5000 transaction detail. As a result: (i) Feb/Mar transaction detail for 6300 Travel and 6400 Marketing Programs was NOT retrieved; (ii) the Stackline SC-M-2203 support document behind JE-00258 was NOT opened; (iii) no bank-side corroboration was performed. Recommended next step: re-run list_transactions for accounts 6300 and 6400 (US, periods 2026-02 and 2026-03), open the support on each March entry, and re-run this flux after depreciation, prepaid amortization and payroll accrual entries are posted. I'd rather hand you an honest partial than a flux with invented drivers for Travel and Marketing."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 10}
